    "text": "In the case of De Silava Vs Sangadasa 40 NLR 162 it was held that where in a partition actioncompensation for improvements due to a bona fide possessor is determined, he has the right to retain possession but it is until the compensation due to him is paid and that it is not necessary to expressly reserved the jus retentionis in the decree.",
